# StoreFlow POS project rule

- Read `CLAUDE.md` before planning or changing this repository; it is the detailed
  architecture, status, scope, command, and handoff source of truth.
- Preserve the offline-first Windows Flutter/Riverpod/GoRouter/Drift architecture.
- Never reset the database or edit `app_database.g.dart` manually. Use an additive
  schema-version migration plus a data-preservation test.
- Enforce permissions in repositories/services as well as UI, and scope business
  queries to the active store.
- Use `Money` integer minor units for financial logic; convert legacy REAL values
  only at persistence boundaries.
- Every stock mutation requires a `stock_movements` row in the same transaction.
- Checkout and future purchase/refund/void workflows must be atomic and audited.
- Do not seed fake production data or claim placeholder modules are implemented.
- Keep desktop UI compact and verify it at 1280×720.
- After material changes run format, analyze, tests, and Windows release build.
